sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Customer
    participant API as REST API
    participant Booking as Booking Service
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    Customer->>API: POST /bookings + Idempotency-Key
    API->>API: Authenticate, validate, normalize, fingerprint
    API->>DB: Lookup (user_id, key)

    alt Existing key, same fingerprint, completed
        DB-->>API: Stored status and response
        API-->>Customer: Replay original result
    else Existing key, different fingerprint
        DB-->>API: Conflicting fingerprint
        API-->>Customer: 409 IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REUSED
    else New logical request
        API->>Booking: Execute create booking
        Booking->>DB: BEGIN + claim idempotency key
        Booking->>DB: Validate concert and categories
        Booking->>DB: Reserve inventory in sorted order (conditional UPDATE)

        alt Sold out
            DB-->>Booking: 0 rows updated
            Booking->>DB: ROLLBACK
            Booking-->>API: INSUFFICIENT_TICKET_INVENTORY
            API-->>Customer: 409 Conflict
        else Inventory reserved
            opt Voucher supplied
                Booking->>DB: Validate scope and reserve quota/redemption
                alt Voucher rejected
                    DB-->>Booking: Ineligible or exhausted
                    Booking->>DB: ROLLBACK inventory and idempotency claim
                    Booking-->>API: VOUCHER_INVALID
                    API-->>Customer: 422 Unprocessable Entity
                else Voucher accepted
                    DB-->>Booking: Discount snapshot
                end
            end
            Booking->>DB: Insert booking, items, prices, history, replay result
            Booking->>DB: COMMIT
            Booking-->>API: Booking response
            API-->>Customer: 201 Created
        end
    end

    Note over Booking,DB: No external network call occurs inside the transaction.
